It had been a while since I'd played Nethack, but someone tempted
me, and after few false starts, I found myself randomly playing a female
chaotic Elvish ranger who turned out to make good.

The game was largely unremarkable (other than it being my first 
ranger through the Quest), except for some mistakes I made by being
rusty. The most serious of these were probably:

* Genociding "mind flayer" and forgetting that there are also
  master mind flayers
* Going hand-to-hand with a master mind flayer in gehennom and
  forgetting a whole lot
* Killing Rodney before I'd found the dungeon bottom and the
  vibrating square (got excited :).

On the plus side, this was on a public server, and I got my GDSM
from a bones level. The only wishes I ever got were from the /oW
in the castle.  It took me forever to get fire resistance; in the
end, I kept praying until I got crowned in order to get it.

Oddly, in the endgame, I never encountered any of the Riders (I saw
Famine telepathically on the right, but went up the middle and never
met one; maybe my guardian angel did for him?)  Got the right altar on
the first go.

